    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2bd20c4957ee5f1e77643e8b7f1c10184db462b0e2a0c9dcfac4debdee9fe378",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source contrasts the earlier workflow of computing all polynomial roots and transferring coefficient errors through an Ostrowski theorem with a Sturm-count workflow surrounded by layered diagnostics: chaotic cross-degree endpoint-sign changes and implausible count drops trigger higher precision, restored neighboring-degree counts test the repair, and a separately located complex zero is retained only as an extra check.",
