    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3114bd92c69a9ed53a1de1f8a2ed463ffdabcc531c78e72900d3c9f59e6b9209",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At a fixed parameter, the source composes an obstruction pipeline: transform moments form finite Jensen polynomials; a non-real polynomial zero places the parameter below the de Bruijn-Newman threshold; Sturm variation counts test the needed non-real-root predicate without recovering every root; and tail and series truncation, even-integrand trapezoidal refinement, interval enlargement, and precision escalation support the numerical inputs, while a Newton-computed complex zero remains a corroborating check.",
